<title>USA: Republic Industries buys Ohio car dealer.</title>
<headline>Republic Industries buys Ohio car dealer.</headline>
<dateline>FORT LAUDERDALE, Fla. 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Republic Industries Inc said Thursday it signed a definitive agreement to buy John Lance Ford of Westlake, Ohio for about $19 million in Republic common stock.</p>
<p>According to Republic, John Lance Ford is one of the nation's oldest Ford dealerships to be held by the same family. It had 1996 revenue of about $65 million.</p>
<p>The acquisition will be accounted for under the purchase method of accounting and is subject to certain manufacturer and government approvals.</p>
</text>
